  "authoringNote": "R09 first-condition routing and metadata quarantine; no supersession, so no version-recovery deferral. Four supporting notes, each v1 of kind supporting_note. Note q (f08x4-note-q) has metadata subject SYN-OTH-F08X4, not the case, so D3 quarantines it by metadata: R02 is conflict for the administrative_reviewer (needs_human_review) with R02.document_quarantined for binding.metadata_subject naming f08x4-note-q v1, parent [f08x4-note-q v1], and the quarantine list is [f08x4-note-q v1]. Its contentHash also mismatches, but R02 alone reports metadata-quarantined versions, so R09 names nothing for q. R09 reports the first applicable condition per version in the order access_restricted, hash_mismatch, access_unreadable, mime_unsupported, body_invalid, kind_mismatch, locator_unresolved. Note h has the case subject and a contentHash of separately specified alternate bytes; its held body is a valid order-kind body, but hash_mismatch precedes kind_mismatch, so h yields only R09.hash_mismatch (conflict, administrative_reviewer, needs_human_review). Note m is text/plain with a matching hash and non-JSON bytes: R09.mime_unsupported only, before body_invalid (unreadable, authorization_coordinator, needs_information). Note u declares accessStatus unreadable with a matching hash and non-JSON bytes: R09.access_unreadable only, since declared access precedes parsing (unreadable, authorization_coordinator, needs_information). The R09 finding is conflict for the administrative_reviewer; the coordinator conditions are retained beneath it. Conditions are serialized by key (access_unreadable, hash_mismatch, mime_unsupported), not by selected status. The C07 parent is the union of condition documents [f08x4-note-h v1, f08x4-note-m v1, f08x4-note-u v1] by document ID, not only h. No note is usable, so no note supplies a fact or citation. R01, R03, R04 and R05 pass on the final order, encounter, receipt and supplier record with the standard citation sets (8, 9, 6, 4); R02 cites the order, encounter and receipt beneficiary name and identifier (6). R06 is manual_review for the qualified_clinical_reviewer with R06.clinical_review (no refs, effect none) and cites the five /clinical/ statements of the usable encounter; R07 passes citing /lcmpReport/incorporated (false; the null evaluationDate is not cited); R08 passes; R10 is not_applicable with R10.pure_assessment. clinicalReviewRequired is true. Every other parent is empty; the superseded list is empty. State needs_human_review. Recorded reading: a rule cites evidence-field facts only from the documents it reads, and R04 reads only final current usable records; every usable encounter and order here is final, so no draft is excluded. The standard chronology holds: the order date 2026-09-08 is after the 2026-08-24 encounter (not the same day, so C02 does not apply) and inside the C01 bound 2027-02-24, and the receipt at 2026-09-09T16:30:00Z is after the C06 span of the order date, which ends 2026-09-09T12:00Z.",
